{"text": "Jamie Hensley 8\n\nGua oxen Nise MITE Treads OND\nDate: June 23, 2020\n\nLarry D. Burks, Township Administrator\n\u2018West Chester Township\n9113 Cincinnati-Dayton Rd\nWest Chester, OH 45069\n\nDear Mr. Burks:\n\nIhave had the great privilege of serving the community of West Chester and the employees of West Chester Township for\nnearly twenty-one years, and for that I am eternally grateful. I have had the opportunity to lead and work alongside countless\nindividuals of excellence in the police department and the public. So it is with deep sadness that I must tender my\nresignation and notice of retirement, effective immediately. I believe this is the only option left that protects my family, my\nhealth, and my career without compromising my values. It is unfortunate to have been treated this way for taking a\nprincipled stance and others may fear coming forward in the future as a result, Please let this letter serve as my formal\n\nretirement from the Department effective immediately.\n\nSincerely,\n\n| eae Neco\n\nJamie L. Hensley\n\nCaptain, West Chester Police Department",
